From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:33:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Translate the Remix menus: zh-CN, zh-TW, ja, ko, fr, ru

The menus (Alt+X) and the descriptions of the options they show can be
read in Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Japanese, Korean, French
and Russian. rtx.gui.language (English by default, a user setting) picks
the language from a combo at the top of both menus; it applies at the
next frame.

- i18n/: remix.pot (English, extracted from the sources by
  tools/update_strings.py) and one UTF-8 .po file per language, 3,293
  messages each. tools/embed.py runs in the build, checks the files
  (printf formats, glyph coverage) and builds them into the runtime, so
  an edited .po is in the next build without code changes.
- ImGui (vendored 1.88, NV-DXVK blocks): one translator hook where text
  is drawn and measured, after IDs are hashed from the English, and
  CJK line breaking in CalcWordWrapPositionA.
- rtx_fork_i18n.cpp: the translator, the language switch, the font
  atlas (only the selected language's glyphs: Noto Sans SC/TC/JP/KR
  subsets in i18n/fonts, SIL OFL 1.1, merged at NVIDIA Sans' em size)
  and the selector. Section headers capitalise the translation.
- Composed readouts in the graphics settings window use printf formats,
  so they translate too; docs/fork-touchpoints.md lists every upstream
  file touched. RtxOptions.md regenerated for the two new options.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
