@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# Translations of the Remix menus
+
+The Remix menus (Alt+X: the graphics settings window and the developer menu) can be shown in
+Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Japanese, Korean, French and Russian. The language is the
+first setting of the graphics settings window's General tab, and sits at the top of the developer
+menu. It is the option `rtx.gui.language` (`en`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`, `ja`, `ko`, `fr`, `ru`; English by
+default), a user setting: **Save Settings** keeps it in `user.conf`.
+
+Translated are the menus' labels, buttons, headers, combo entries, messages and tooltips, and the
+descriptions of the `rtx.*` options the menus show (the first part of an option's tooltip). Text the
+code puts together at run time, values, names of mods, textures and layers, and the config option
+names stay as they are.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| `remix.pot` | The English text, extracted from the sources. Generated: do not edit |
+| `zh-CN.po`, `zh-TW.po`, `ja.po`, `ko.po`, `fr.po`, `ru.po` | One UTF-8 file per language: each English `msgid` with its `msgstr` |
+| `fonts/NotoSans{SC,TC,JP,KR}.otf` | Chinese, Japanese and Korean glyphs (NVIDIA Sans has Latin and Cyrillic); `fonts/OFL.txt` is their licence |
+| `tools/update_strings.py` | Extracts the text into `remix.pot` and merges it into every `.po` |
+| `tools/embed.py` | Run by the build: checks the `.po` files and builds them into the runtime |
+| `tools/subset_fonts.py` | Rebuilds the fonts from the full Noto Sans fonts (needs fontTools) |
+
+## Reviewing and editing a translation
+
+Edit the language's `.po` file in any text editor (UTF-8) or a PO editor such as Poedit. An entry:
+
+```po
+#. option rtx.enableRaytracing
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_options.h:612
+msgid "Enables or disables ray tracing."
+msgstr "启用或禁用光线追踪。"
+```
+
+- `#.` names the option whose tooltip this is; `#:` is where the text is in the sources.
+- Change `msgstr` only. Long text may continue on following lines, each a `"..."` string; `\n` is a
+  line break, `\"` a quote, `\\` a backslash.
+- An empty `msgstr` shows the English. `#, fuzzy` above an entry also keeps the English, until you
+  remove the flag.
+- `#, c-format` marks a printf format: keep every `%d`, `%s`, `%.2f`, ... in the same order, and
+  write a percent sign as `%%`.
+
+Rebuild the runtime as usual (`meson compile -C _CompRelease_x64`). The build runs
+`tools/embed.py`, so the edited text is in the next `d3d9.dll`; no code changes. When a translation
+breaks a rule, the build stops and names the file and line, for example
+`error: i18n/ja.po:1234: printf conversions ['%d'] must match the English ['%d', '%s']`.
+
+To check the files without building:
+
+```powershell
+python i18n\tools\embed.py --pot i18n\remix.pot --latin-font external\fonts\NVIDIASans\NVIDIASansMd.ttf `
+  --fonts-dir i18n\fonts --out $env:TEMP\rtx_i18n_check.cpp i18n\zh-CN.po i18n\zh-TW.po i18n\ja.po i18n\ko.po i18n\fr.po i18n\ru.po
+```
+
+## A character the font does not have
+
+The Chinese, Japanese and Korean fonts hold a common character set of each language (GB 2312;
+the frequent Big5 characters; JIS X 0208; the 2,350 hangul syllables of KS X 1001) and every
+character the translations use. A translation with another character stops the build with
+`... have no glyph for '...' (U+....)`. Add it to the font:
+
+```powershell
+python -m pip install fonttools
+python i18n\tools\subset_fonts.py --source-dir <folder with Noto Sans SC, TC, JP and KR Regular .otf>
+```
+
+The source fonts are Noto Sans SC, TC, JP and KR Regular (OTF), from
+<https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk> or the copies in SteamVR's
+`tools\steamvr_environments\game\steamtours\panorama\fonts` (the default when SteamVR is installed).
+French and Russian use NVIDIA Sans, which has Latin-1, Latin Extended-A and Cyrillic, but no
+arrows or math symbols.
+
+The menus' font atlas holds only the glyphs of the selected language (and of the language names),
+so a CJK language costs a few MB of video memory, and English nothing extra.
+
+## When the sources change
+
+New or changed menu text is not translated until it is in the `.po` files:
+
+```powershell
+python i18n\tools\update_strings.py
+```
+
+It rewrites `remix.pot` from the sources and merges it into every `.po`: existing translations stay,
+new text gets an empty `msgstr` (shown in English until translated), and text that left the sources
+moves to the end of the file as `#~` entries, so a translation is never lost. `--check` only reports
+whether `remix.pot` is current.
+
+To see which text on screen has no translation, start the game with the environment variable
+`RTX_GUI_LOG_UNTRANSLATED_TEXT=1` (or `rtx.gui.logUntranslatedText = True`): each untranslated text
+is written once to `rtx-remix\logs\remix-dxvk.log` as `[i18n] untranslated (<language>): "..."`.
+
+## Adding a language
+
+1. `python i18n\tools\update_strings.py --new-language de --name Deutsch` (with `--font NotoSansSC`
+   or another font of `fonts\` when NVIDIA Sans lacks its letters) starts `de.po`.
+2. Add `'../../i18n/de.po'` to `rtx_i18n_po_files` in `src/dxvk/meson.build`.
+3. Translate, build. The language appears in the language combo under the name given.
+
+## How it works
+
+ImGui (`src/dxvk/imgui`) asks a translator for every text it draws or measures; the translator
+(`src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_fork_i18n.cpp`) swaps an English text for its translation. Widget IDs keep
+hashing the English, so window positions, open headers and `imgui.ini` do not depend on the
+language. printf formats are swapped before formatting, only for translations with the same
+conversions. A language change rebuilds the font atlas with that language's glyphs.
