+msgid "Surface Style"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:160
+msgid "Procedural surface preset. Knobs below tune the chosen style."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:162
+msgid "Crater Density"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:169 src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:1109
+msgid "Detail"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:182
+msgid "Combined surface detail: smooth/coarse <- 0.0 ... 1.0 (default) ... 2.0 -> punchy/fine. Drives Surface Contrast and Surface Noise Scale via a two-segment linear curve. Power users can .conf-tune surfaceContrast / surfaceNoiseScale individually for off-curve combinations."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:186
+msgid "Dark Side Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:198
+msgid "Sun"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:202
+msgid "Sun Size"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:204
+msgid "Angular diameter of the sun light in degrees (Earth's sun is ~0.545 deg). The light's half-angle = Sun Size / 2, which sets shadow softness and the sun's size in reflective highlights. Numos draws no separate sun disc. Greyed out while Shadow Softness > 0 (the override owns the half-angle)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:211
+msgid "Shadow Softness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:213
+msgid "Override for the sun light's angular half-angle, in degrees. 0 = physical: track Sun Size / 2 (leave here unless you need the override). When > 0 it owns the half-angle and Sun Size greys out - larger = softer penumbra. Kept separate from Sun Size so a game/API-driven physical sun size can stay untouched while shadows are art-directed."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:220
+msgid "Sun Intensity"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:221
+msgid "Strength of Sun"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:231
+#, c-format
+msgid "Sun Elevation   %7.2f deg"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:232
+#, c-format
+msgid "Sun Rotation    %7.2f deg"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:234
+msgid "Driven by the Time Cycle below. Disable it to control the sun directly again."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:236
+msgid "Sun Elevation"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:237
+msgid "Sun angle from horizon"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:239
+msgid "Sun Rotation"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:240
+msgid "Rotation of sun around zenith"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:244
+msgid "Flip Up Axis"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:246
+msgid ""
+"Fixes a sky rendered exactly upside down - bright zenith beneath you, dark ground half overhead - in games whose up axis points the opposite way to what Remix assumes.\n"
+"\n"
+"NOT the fix for a sky that looks rotated or sideways; that is rtx.zUp not matching the game. To tell them apart: turn the Time Cycle off, set Sun Elevation to about 45, and look straight up. Zenith off to one side = zUp problem. Zenith under your feet = this.\n"
+"\n"
+"Also reverses the direction the sun travels across the sky - flipping which way is up reverses the sense of rotation seen from the new zenith. Sun Rotation / North Offset move where the arc sits but cannot undo that."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:255
+msgid "Time Cycle"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:256
+msgid "Enable Time Cycle"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:258
+msgid "Drive the sun from a Remix-side clock instead of Sun Elevation / Sun Rotation. The intended workflow is for the game to push the sun through the Remix API, but plenty of games have no day/night cycle to push - this gives them one. While enabled it OWNS the sun direction, and Sun Elevation / Sun Rotation (including API pushes) are ignored."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:266
+#, c-format
+msgid "Current time    %02d:%02d"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:268
+msgid "Time Of Day"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:270
+msgid "Hours, 0-24. 12 is solar noon. While the cycle runs this is the START time and editing it re-seeds the running clock; while the cycle is off it places the sun directly, so it doubles as a manual time-of-day control."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:274
+msgid "Day Length"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:276
+msgid "Real-world minutes for one full 24-hour cycle. 24 gives a minute per in-game hour."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:278
+msgid "Latitude"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:280
+msgid "Observer latitude, positive north. Sets how high the sun climbs and how tilted its arc is: 0 sends it near-vertically overhead, high latitudes keep it low with long shallow sunrises and sunsets."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:284
+msgid "Day Of Year"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:286
+msgid "Sets the solar declination, i.e. the season. 80 = March equinox (due-east sunrise, 12-hour day), 172 = June solstice, 355 = December solstice."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:289
+msgid "North Offset"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:291
+msgid "Rotates the whole solar arc so the model's north matches the game world's. Adjust until sunrise arrives from the direction the game treats as east."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:303
+msgid "Stars"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:304
+msgid "Star Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:306
+msgid "Star Density"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:308
+msgid "Threshold: 0 = all stars visible, 1 = no stars."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:309
+msgid "Star Twinkle Speed"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:317
+msgid "Milky Way"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:320
+msgid "Master toggle for galactic-band effects: in-band density boost, band-specific star colors, and the diffuse background glow. When off, stars distribute uniformly."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:322
+msgid "Density Boost"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:325
+msgid "Extra star density inside the galactic band. Higher = more (dim) band stars."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:326
+msgid "Glow Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:329
+msgid "Diffuse band-glow brightness (the soft dust haze across the Milky Way). 0 disables the glow."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:330
+msgid "Outer Color"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:332
+msgid "Cool outer-edge tint of the band (where young stars dominate). Default cool blue."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:333
+msgid "Core Color"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:336
+msgid "Warm bright-core tint at the galactic center. Default warm cream/yellow. HDR — values above 1.0 push beyond LDR gamut for a brighter core."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:340
+msgid "Dust Amount"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:343
+msgid "How strongly dust patches darken the glow. 0 = no dust, 1 = full dust contrast."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:350
+msgid "Star Appearance"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:351
+msgid "Star PSF Sharpness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:354
+msgid "Gaussian PSF exponent. Lower = bigger softer stars, higher = sharper pinpoints."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:355
+msgid "Star Cloud Extinction Power"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:358
+msgid "Exponent on cloud view-transmittance when extincting stars. Higher = stars die through clouds faster."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:359
+msgid "Star Ambient Coupling"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:362
+msgid "Star/airglow coupling into cloud-march nightLight, as a multiple of the calibrated night level (1.0 = calibrated, ~2 doubles it). 0 = disabled."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:370
+msgid "Global Lighting"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:372
+msgid "Atmospheric Coupling"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:376
+msgid "Multiplier on the moon's contribution to atmospheric scattering. 0 = no blue-dome around the moon; 1 = default; >1 = exaggerated."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:385
+msgid "Surface Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:388
+msgid "Moonlight level on the ground / scene (surface path only; clouds are Cloud Brightness below). Default 50 is the FNV tonemapper calibration. The conf-only moonNeeStrength master scales both paths and is driven by weather presets."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:393
+msgid "Cloud Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:396
+msgid "Overall cloud-moon lighting: the directional silver-lining term AND the ambient airglow together. For forward-glow emphasis only, use Silver Lining Intensity (Cloud-Look & Halo Shape) instead of stacking this."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:406
+msgid "Cloud-Look & Halo Shape"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:407
+msgid "Silver Lining Intensity"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:410
+msgid "Forward-glow emphasis ONLY: scales the directional silver-lining term (Lambert diffuse + HG phase) in front of the moon and nothing else. The overall cloud-moon level (incl. airglow) is Cloud Brightness (Global Lighting) - set that first, then emphasize here. 0 = no silver lining. Diffuse-vs-phase ratio: .conf moonCloudDiffuseGain / moonCloudPhaseGain."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:417
+msgid "Silver Lining Sharpness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:420
+msgid "Tightness of the silver-lining glow peak. Higher = sharper pinpoint; lower = softer falloff. Henyey-Greenstein g for cloud-moon forward scatter. Default 0.85."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:423
+msgid "Halo Glow"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:426
+msgid "MASTER over the moon's glow: scales the disk halo AND the cloud ambient airglow together. 0 = no halo / airglow. 1 = default. Halo-vs-airglow ratio: Halo Brightness below (halo-only trim), or .conf moonHaloMagnitude / moonAmbientAirglow."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:433
+msgid "Halo Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:436
+msgid "Halo-only trim under the Halo Glow master: scales the disk halo Gaussian WITHOUT touching the cloud airglow - sets the halo : airglow ratio. Default 15 is the FNV tonemapper calibration (1 = physically pure)."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:554
+msgid ""
+"Skybox Rasterization: Traditional skybox rendering\n"
+"Numos: Hillaire atmospheric scattering"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_atmosphere_ui.cpp:557
+msgid "Sky Brightness"
+msgstr ""
+
