+msgstr "Закрепить и заморозить для настройки"
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1152
+msgid "Snap the blender to this preset (0 s blend) and freeze variation so edits show on a held image. Unchecking restores the previous variation intensity."
+msgstr "Мгновенно переключить смешивание на этот пресет (смешивание 0 s) и заморозить вариацию, чтобы правки отображались на неизменном изображении. Снятие флажка восстанавливает прежнюю интенсивность вариации."
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1170
+msgid "Copy Into Edited"
+msgstr "Копировать в редактируемый"
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1172
+msgid "Copy every value from the chosen preset into the one being edited."
+msgstr "Скопировать все значения из выбранного пресета в редактируемый."
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1174
+msgid "Snapshot Live -> Preset"
+msgstr "Текущие значения -> пресет"
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1176
+msgid "Capture the current live renderer values into this preset. Tune the real atmosphere/volumetrics with the blender dormant, then capture."
+msgstr "Записать текущие значения рендерера в этот пресет. Настройте настоящую атмосферу/объёмные эффекты при неактивном смешивании, затем выполните запись."
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1179
+msgid "Copy as user.conf lines"
+msgstr "Копировать как строки user.conf"
+
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_weather.cpp:1183
+msgid "Optional: copies this preset as rtx.weather.preset.* lines to the clipboard. The dev menu's Save Settings already persists edits to the modder config; use this only to move values into a specific game's user.conf."
+msgstr "Необязательно: копирует этот пресет в буфер обмена в виде строк rtx.weather.preset.*. Кнопка «Сохранить» в меню разработчика уже сохраняет правки в конфигурацию мода; используйте это, только чтобы перенести значения в user.conf конкретной игры."
+
+#. option rtx.xess.preset
+#: src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_xess.h:53
+msgid "Adjusts XeSS scaling factor, trades quality for performance."
+msgstr "Настраивает коэффициент масштабирования XeSS, жертвуя качеством ради производительности."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.albedoScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:79
+msgid "A scale factor to apply to all albedo values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Коэффициент масштаба для всех значений альбедо в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.albedoBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:80
+msgid "A bias factor to add to all albedo values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Смещение, добавляемое ко всем значениям альбедо в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.roughnessScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:81
+msgid "A scale factor to apply to all roughness values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Коэффициент масштаба для всех значений шероховатости в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.roughnessBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:82
+msgid "A bias factor to add to all roughness values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Смещение, добавляемое ко всем значениям шероховатости в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.metallicScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:83
+msgid "A scale factor to apply to all metallic values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Коэффициент масштаба для всех значений металличности в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.metallicBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:84
+msgid "A bias factor to add to all metallic values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Смещение, добавляемое ко всем значениям металличности в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.normalIntensity
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:85
+msgid "An arbitrary strength scale factor to apply when decoding normals in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Произвольный коэффициент силы, применяемый при декодировании нормалей в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.layeredWaterNormalMotion
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:86
+msgid ""
+"A vector describing the motion in the U and V axes across a texture to apply for layered water.\n"
+"Only takes effect when layered water normals are enabled (and an object is properly classified as animated water)."
+msgstr ""
+"Вектор движения по осям U и V по текстуре для слоистой воды.\n"
+"Действует, только если включены нормали слоистой воды (и объект правильно отнесён к анимированной воде)."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.layeredWaterNormalMotionScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:90
+msgid ""
+"A scale factor applied to the layered water normal motion vector.\n"
+"Only takes effect when layered water normals are enabled (and an object is properly classified as animated water)."
+msgstr ""
+"Коэффициент масштаба вектора движения нормалей слоистой воды.\n"
+"Действует, только если включены нормали слоистой воды (и объект правильно отнесён к анимированной воде)."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.layeredWaterNormalLodBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:93
+msgid ""
+"The LoD bias to use when sampling from the normal map on layered water for the second layer of detail.\n"
+"This value typically should be greater than 0 to allow for a more blurry mip to be selected as this allows for a low frequency variation of normals to be applied to the higher frequency variation from the typical normal map.\n"
+"Only takes effect when layered water normals are enabled (and an object is properly classified as animated water)."
+msgstr ""
+"Смещение LOD при выборке из карты нормалей слоистой воды для второго слоя детализации.\n"
+"Обычно значение должно быть больше 0, чтобы выбирался более размытый MIP-уровень: так низкочастотная вариация нормалей накладывается на высокочастотную вариацию обычной карты нормалей.\n"
+"Действует, только если включены нормали слоистой воды (и объект правильно отнесён к анимированной воде)."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.layeredWaterNormalEnable
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:97
+msgid ""
+"A flag indicating if layered water normal should be enabled or disabled.\n"
+"Note that objects must be properly classified as animated water to be rendered with this mode."
+msgstr ""
+"Флаг включения или отключения нормалей слоистой воды.\n"
+"Обратите внимание: чтобы рендериться в этом режиме, объекты должны быть правильно отнесены к анимированной воде."
+
+#. option rtx.opaqueMaterial.enableThinFilmOverride
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:104
+msgid "A flag to force the thin-film layer on the opaque material to be enabled. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Флаг принудительного включения слоя тонкой плёнки у непрозрачного материала. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.transmittanceColorScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:135
+msgid "A scale factor to apply to all transmittance color values in the translucent material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Коэффициент масштаба для всех значений цвета пропускания в полупрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.transmittanceColorBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:136
+msgid "A bias factor to add to all transmittance color values in the opaque material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Смещение, добавляемое ко всем значениям цвета пропускания в непрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.normalIntensity
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:137
+msgid "An arbitrary strength scale factor to apply when decoding normals in the translucent material. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Произвольный коэффициент силы, применяемый при декодировании нормалей в полупрозрачном материале. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.refractiveIndexScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:138
+msgid "A scale factor to apply to the index of refraction for all translucent materials. The scale is clamped to [0.0, 3.0]. Should only be used for look development."
+msgstr "Коэффициент масштаба показателя преломления для всех полупрозрачных материалов. Масштаб ограничен диапазоном [0.0, 3.0]. Используйте только для разработки внешнего вида."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.animatedWaterPrimaryNormalMotion
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:141
+msgid ""
+"Velocity in UV space for the primary texture coordinate.\n"
+"This relies on Remix animation time, which will not respect any time warping performed by the game (so pause, slow mo, etc will not change animation speed)."
+msgstr ""
+"Скорость в пространстве UV для основной текстурной координаты.\n"
+"Зависит от времени анимации Remix, которое не учитывает изменения хода времени в игре (пауза, замедление и т. п. не меняют скорость анимации)."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.animatedWaterSecondaryNormalMotion
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:144
+msgid ""
+"Velocity in UV space for the secondary texture coordinate.\n"
+"This relies on Remix animation time, which will not respect any time warping performed by the game (so pause, slow mo, etc will not change animation speed)."
+msgstr ""
+"Скорость в пространстве UV для дополнительной текстурной координаты.\n"
+"Зависит от времени анимации Remix, которое не учитывает изменения хода времени в игре (пауза, замедление и т. п. не меняют скорость анимации)."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.animatedWaterSecondaryNormalLodBias
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:147
+msgid ""
+"LoD bias to use when taking the second normal map sample.\n"
+"Values greater than 0 will cause the secondary normal map to be blurred, resulting in lower frequency waves."
+msgstr ""
+"Смещение LOD для второй выборки из карты нормалей.\n"
+"Значения больше 0 размывают вторичную карту нормалей, что даёт более низкочастотные волны."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.animatedWaterEnable
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:150
+msgid ""
+"If enabled, draw calls in the AnimatedWater category and a translucent material will have their primary texcoordinates animated, and will also take a second sample from the normal map.\n"
+"Note that objects must be properly categorized as animated water to be rendered with this mode."
+msgstr ""
+"Если включено, у вызовов отрисовки из категории AnimatedWater с полупрозрачным материалом анимируются основные текстурные координаты и берётся вторая выборка из карты нормалей.\n"
+"Обратите внимание: чтобы рендериться в этом режиме, объекты должны быть правильно отнесены к анимированной воде."
+
+#. option rtx.translucentMaterial.enableDiffuseLayerOverride
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/material_args.h:155
+msgid "A flag to force the diffuse layer on the translucent material to be enabled. Should only be used for debugging or development."
+msgstr "Флаг принудительного включения диффузного слоя у полупрозрачного материала. Используйте только для отладки или разработки."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.distanceMode
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:73
+msgid "The view distance mode, None disables view distance, Hard Cutoff will cut off geometry past a point, Coherent Noise will feather geometry out using a stable worldspace noise pattern (experimental), and Coherent Noise Smooth Primary will do the same except for primary rays, which instead smoothly blend distant surfaces into the sky."
+msgstr "Режим дальности прорисовки: «Нет» отключает ограничение дальности, «Жёсткая отсечка» отсекает геометрию дальше определённой точки, «Когерентный шум» плавно растворяет геометрию с помощью стабильного шумового шаблона в мировом пространстве (экспериментально), а «Когерентный шум, плавные первичные» делает то же самое, кроме первичных лучей, для которых далёкие поверхности плавно смешиваются с небом."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.distanceFunction
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:74
+msgid "The view distance function. 0: Euclidean, a simple distance from the camera. 1: Horizontal (Planar Euclidean), which ignores distance across the world's \"up\" direction. 2: Vertical, which uses only the \"up\" direction."
+msgstr "Функция дальности прорисовки. 0: «Евклидова» — простое расстояние от камеры. 1: «По горизонтали» (плоское евклидово), без учёта расстояния вдоль направления «вверх» мира. 2: «По вертикали» — только вдоль направления «вверх»."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.distanceThreshold
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:75
+msgid "The view distance to draw out to based on the result of the view distance function, only used for the Hard Cutoff view distance mode."
+msgstr "Дальность прорисовки по результату функции дальности; используется только в режиме «Жёсткая отсечка»."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.distanceFadeMin
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:78
+msgid "The view distance based on the result of the view distance function to start view distance noise fading at, only used for the Coherent Noise view distance mode."
+msgstr "Дальность по результату функции дальности, с которой начинается шумовое затухание; используется только в режиме «Когерентный шум»."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.distanceFadeMax
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:81
+msgid "The view distance based on the result of the view distance function to end view distance noise fading at (and effectively draw nothing past this point), only used for the Coherent Noise view distance mode."
+msgstr "Дальность по результату функции дальности, на которой заканчивается шумовое затухание (дальше этой точки фактически ничего не рисуется); используется только в режиме «Когерентный шум»."
+
+#. option rtx.viewDistance.noiseScale
+#: src/dxvk/shaders/rtx/pass/view_distance_args.h:83
+msgid "The scale per meter value applied to ther world space position fed into the noise generation function for generating the fade in Coherent Noise view distance mode."
+msgstr "Масштаб на метр, применяемый к позиции в мировом пространстве, передаваемой в функцию генерации шума для затухания в режиме «Когерентный шум»."
+
+#~ msgid "%.1f GB"
+#~ msgstr "%.1f GB"
+
+#~ msgid "%+d.0 EV"
+#~ msgstr "%+d.0 EV"
+
+#~ msgid "%+.2f EV"
+#~ msgstr "%+.2f EV"
+
+#~ msgid "%+.1f EV"
+#~ msgstr "%+.1f EV"
diff --git a/i18n/tools/embed.py b/i18n/tools/embed.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cda752e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/i18n/tools/embed.py
@@ -0,0 +1,174 @@
+"""Builds the menu translations into the runtime: reads i18n/remix.pot and the i18n/<language>.po
+files, checks them, and writes the C++ tables declared in src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_fork_i18n_data.h.
+
+The build (src/dxvk/meson.build) runs it whenever one of its inputs changes, so an edited .po file
+reaches the next build without code changes. Run by hand to check translations without building:
+
+    python i18n/tools/embed.py --pot i18n/remix.pot --latin-font <NVIDIASansMd.ttf>
+        --fonts-dir i18n/fonts --out <file.cpp> i18n/zh-CN.po ...
+
+A translation is used when its msgstr is not empty and the entry is not marked fuzzy. Errors stop
+the build: printf conversions that differ from the English of a format string, "##", characters
+neither NVIDIA Sans nor the language's font (X-Remix-Font in the .po header) can draw.
+Exit codes: 0 success, 1 errors in the translations, 2 bad command line.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import os
+import sys
+
+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
+import fontcmap  # noqa: E402
+import po  # noqa: E402
+
+
+def c_bytes(name: str, data: bytes, static: bool) -> str:
+    if not data:
+        data = b"\0"
+    rows = [",".join(str(b) for b in data[i:i + 40]) for i in range(0, len(data), 40)]
+    body = ",\n".join(rows)
+    return f"{'static ' if static else ''}const unsigned char {name}[] = {{\n{body}\n}};\n"
+
+
+def c_string(text: str) -> str:
+    out = []
+    for b in text.encode("utf-8"):
+        if 0x20 <= b < 0x7F and chr(b) not in '"\\?':
+            out.append(chr(b))
+        else:
+            out.append(f'\\x{b:02x}""')
+    return '"' + "".join(out) + '"'
+
+
+def main() -> int:
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
+    ap.add_argument("--pot", required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--latin-font", required=True, help="NVIDIA Sans, the menus' main font")
+    ap.add_argument("--fonts-dir", required=True, help="folder of the fonts named by X-Remix-Font")
+    ap.add_argument("--out", required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("po_files", nargs="+")
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+
+    errors = []
+    warnings = []
+    _, pot_entries = po.parse(args.pot)
+    english = [e.msgid for e in pot_entries]
+    index = {msgid: i for i, msgid in enumerate(english)}
+    c_format = {e.msgid for e in pot_entries if "c-format" in e.flags}
+    if len(english) > 0xFFFF:
+        errors.append(f"{args.pot}: more than 65535 messages")
+
+    latin_chars = fontcmap.characters(args.latin_font)
+    font_chars = {}
+    font_metrics = {}
+    languages = []
+    for path in args.po_files:
+        header, entries = po.parse(path)
+        fields = po.header_fields(header)
+        code = fields.get("Language", "")
+        name = fields.get("X-Remix-Language-Name", "")
+        font = fields.get("X-Remix-Font", "")
+        if not code or not name:
+            errors.append(f"{path}: the header needs Language and X-Remix-Language-Name")
+            continue
+        allowed = set(latin_chars) | {0x0A, 0x09}
+        if font:
+            font_path = os.path.join(args.fonts_dir, font + ".otf")
+            if not os.path.exists(font_path):
+                errors.append(f"{path}: X-Remix-Font {font}: no file {font_path}")
+                continue
+            if font not in font_chars:
+                font_chars[font] = fontcmap.characters(font_path)
+                font_metrics[font] = fontcmap.height_per_em(font_path)
+            allowed |= font_chars[font]
+        for c in name:
+            if ord(c) not in allowed:
+                errors.append(f"{path}: X-Remix-Language-Name: no glyph for {c!r} (U+{ord(c):04X})")
+
+        records = bytearray()
+        count = 0
+        for e in entries:
+            if e.obsolete or not e.msgstr or "fuzzy" in e.flags:
+                continue
+            where = f"{path}:{e.line}"
+            if e.msgid not in index:
+                warnings.append(f"{where}: warning: not in remix.pot (run i18n/tools/update_strings.py); skipped")
+                continue
+            text = e.msgstr
+            specs_match = po.format_specs(text) == po.format_specs(e.msgid)
+            format_safe = specs_match and not po.stray_percent(text)
+            if e.msgid in c_format and not format_safe:
+                errors.append(f"{where}: printf conversions {po.format_specs(text)} must match the English "
+                              f"{po.format_specs(e.msgid)} (write a percent sign as %%)")
+                continue
+            if "##" in text:
+                errors.append(f"{where}: a translation must not contain ##")
+                continue
+            if "\0" in text:
+                errors.append(f"{where}: a translation must not contain a NUL character")
+                continue
+            missing = sorted({c for c in text if ord(c) not in allowed})
+            if missing:
+                font_note = f"NVIDIA Sans and {font}" if font else "NVIDIA Sans"
+                listed = " ".join(f"{c!r} (U+{ord(c):04X})" for c in missing)
+                errors.append(f"{where}: {font_note} have no glyph for {listed}"
+                              + ("; see i18n/README.md to add characters to the font" if font else ""))
+                continue
+            i = index[e.msgid]
+            records += bytes((i & 0xFF, i >> 8, 1 if format_safe else 0)) + text.encode("utf-8") + b"\0"
+            count += 1
+        languages.append((code, name, font, bytes(records), count, path))
+
+    for w in warnings:
+        print(w, file=sys.stderr)
+    if errors:
+        for err in errors:
+            print(f"error: {err}", file=sys.stderr)
+        print(f"i18n: {len(errors)} errors in the translations; nothing was written", file=sys.stderr)
+        return 1
+
+    out = ["// Generated by i18n/tools/embed.py from i18n/remix.pot and i18n/*.po. Do not edit: edit the .po files.",
+           '#include "rtx_render/rtx_fork_i18n_data.h"',
+           "",
+           "namespace dxvk {",
+           "namespace i18n_data {",
+           ""]
+    english_bytes = b"".join(m.encode("utf-8") + b"\0" for m in english)
+    out.append(c_bytes("kEnglish", english_bytes, static=False))
+    out.append(f"const size_t kEnglishSize = {len(english_bytes)};")
+    out.append(f"const uint32_t kMessageCount = {len(english)};")
+    out.append("")
+    for n, (code, name, font, records, count, _) in enumerate(languages):
+        out.append(c_bytes(f"kRecords{n}", records, static=True))
+    out.append("const Language kLanguages[] = {")
+    for n, (code, name, font, records, count, _) in enumerate(languages):
+        out.append(f"  {{ {c_string(code)}, {c_string(name)}, {c_string(font)}, kRecords{n}, {len(records)}, {count} }},")
+    out.append("};")
+    out.append(f"const size_t kLanguageCount = {len(languages)};")
+    out.append("")
+    out.append("const FontMetrics kFontMetrics[] = {")
+    for font, h in sorted(font_metrics.items()):
+        out.append(f"  {{ {c_string(font)}, {h:.6f}f }},")
+    if not font_metrics:
+        out.append('  { "", 1.0f },')
+    out.append("};")
+    out.append(f"const size_t kFontMetricsCount = {len(font_metrics)};")
+    out.append(f"const float kBaseFontHeightPerEm = {fontcmap.height_per_em(args.latin_font):.6f}f;")
+    out.append("")
+    out.append("} // namespace i18n_data")
+    out.append("} // namespace dxvk")
+    out.append("")
+
+    tmp = args.out + ".tmp"
+    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
+        f.write("\n".join(out))
+    os.replace(tmp, args.out)
+    summary = ", ".join(f"{code} {count}/{len(english)}" for code, _, _, _, count, _ in languages)
+    print(f"i18n: {len(english)} messages; translated: {summary}")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main())
diff --git a/i18n/tools/fontcmap.py b/i18n/tools/fontcmap.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c70c1cca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/i18n/tools/fontcmap.py
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+"""Reads the set of characters a TrueType or OpenType font maps (its cmap table).
+
+Standard library only, so the build can check that every translated character has a glyph.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import struct
+
+
+def _tables(data: bytes) -> dict:
+    num_tables = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, 4)[0]
+    tables = {}
+    for i in range(num_tables):
+        tag, _, offset, _ = struct.unpack_from(">4sIII", data, 12 + 16 * i)
+        tables[tag] = offset
+    return tables
+
+
+def height_per_em(path: str) -> float:
+    """(hhea ascender - hhea descender) / unitsPerEm: the line height ImGui sizes a font by, in em."""
+    with open(path, "rb") as f:
+        data = f.read()
+    tables = _tables(data)
+    units_per_em = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, tables[b"head"] + 18)[0]
+    ascender, descender = struct.unpack_from(">hh", data, tables[b"hhea"] + 4)
+    return (ascender - descender) / units_per_em
+
+
+def characters(path: str) -> set:
+    with open(path, "rb") as f:
+        data = f.read()
+    cmap_offset = _tables(data).get(b"cmap")
+    if cmap_offset is None:
+        raise ValueError(f"{path}: no cmap table")
+
+    count = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, cmap_offset + 2)[0]
+    best = None
+    for i in range(count):
+        platform, encoding, offset = struct.unpack_from(">HHI", data, cmap_offset + 4 + 8 * i)
+        fmt = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, cmap_offset + offset)[0]
+        unicode_table = (platform == 0) or (platform == 3 and encoding in (1, 10))
+        if unicode_table and fmt in (4, 12):
+            if best is None or fmt == 12:
+                best = (fmt, cmap_offset + offset)
+    if best is None:
+        raise ValueError(f"{path}: no Unicode cmap subtable of format 4 or 12")
+
+    fmt, base = best
+    chars = set()
+    if fmt == 4:
+        seg_count = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, base + 6)[0] // 2
+        ends = base + 14
+        starts = ends + 2 * seg_count + 2
+        deltas = starts + 2 * seg_count
+        range_offsets = deltas + 2 * seg_count
+        for s in range(seg_count):
+            end = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, ends + 2 * s)[0]
+            start = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, starts + 2 * s)[0]
+            delta = struct.unpack_from(">h", data, deltas + 2 * s)[0]
+            ro = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, range_offsets + 2 * s)[0]
+            for c in range(start, end + 1):
+                if c == 0xFFFF:
+                    continue
+                if ro == 0:
+                    glyph = (c + delta) & 0xFFFF
+                else:
+                    addr = range_offsets + 2 * s + ro + 2 * (c - start)
+                    glyph = struct.unpack_from(">H", data, addr)[0]
+                    if glyph:
+                        glyph = (glyph + delta) & 0xFFFF
+                if glyph:
+                    chars.add(c)
+    else:
+        groups = struct.unpack_from(">I", data, base + 12)[0]
+        for g in range(groups):
+            start, end, glyph = struct.unpack_from(">III", data, base + 16 + 12 * g)
+            for c in range(start, end + 1):
+                if glyph + (c - start):
+                    chars.add(c)
+    return chars
diff --git a/i18n/tools/po.py b/i18n/tools/po.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..41d03fe3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/i18n/tools/po.py
@@ -0,0 +1,212 @@
+"""Reads and writes the gettext PO files of the Remix menu translations.
+
+Only the subset of the PO format the i18n folder uses: msgid/msgstr pairs, the four comment kinds
+(translator "# ", extracted "#.", reference "#:", flags "#,") and obsolete entries ("#~").
+Standard library only, because the build runs it.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import dataclasses
+import re
+
+_ESCAPES = {"n": "\n", "t": "\t", "r": "\r", "a": "\a", "b": "\b", "f": "\f", "v": "\v", "\\": "\\", '"': '"', "'": "'", "?": "?"}
+_NAMED = {"\\": "\\\\", '"': '\\"', "\n": "\\n", "\t": "\\t", "\r": "\\r", "\a": "\\a", "\b": "\\b", "\f": "\\f",
+          "\v": "\\v"}
+
+
+class PoError(Exception):
+    pass
+
+
+@dataclasses.dataclass
+class Entry:
+    msgid: str
+    msgstr: str = ""
+    comments: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)    # "# " translator comments
+    extracted: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)   # "#." notes from the extractor
+    references: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)  # "#:" source locations
+    flags: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)       # "#," flags such as c-format, fuzzy
+    obsolete: bool = False
+    line: int = 0
+
+
+def unescape(body: str, path: str, line: int) -> str:
+    out = []
+    i = 0
+    while i < len(body):
+        c = body[i]
+        if c != "\\":
+            out.append(c)
+            i += 1
+            continue
+        i += 1
+        if i >= len(body):
+            raise PoError(f"{path}:{line}: string ends with a backslash")
+        c = body[i]
+        if c in _ESCAPES:
+            out.append(_ESCAPES[c])
+            i += 1
+        elif c == "x":
+            m = re.match(r"[0-9a-fA-F]{1,2}", body[i + 1:])
+            if not m:
+                raise PoError(f"{path}:{line}: bad \\x escape")
+            out.append(chr(int(m.group(0), 16)))
+            i += 1 + len(m.group(0))
+        elif c in "01234567":
+            m = re.match(r"[0-7]{1,3}", body[i:])
+            out.append(chr(int(m.group(0), 8)))
+            i += len(m.group(0))
+        else:
+            raise PoError(f"{path}:{line}: unknown escape \\{c}")
+    return "".join(out)
+
+
+def escape(text: str) -> str:
+    out = []
+    for c in text:
+        if c in _NAMED:
+            out.append(_NAMED[c])
+        elif ord(c) < 0x20 or ord(c) == 0x7f:
+            out.append("\\%03o" % ord(c))
+        else:
+            out.append(c)
+    return "".join(out)
+
+
+def parse(path: str):
+    """Returns (header, entries). The header is the entry with the empty msgid, or None."""
+    with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8-sig", newline="") as f:
+        lines = [line[:-1] if line.endswith("\r") else line for line in f.read().split("\n")]
+
+    header = None
+    entries = []
+    cur = None          # Entry being built
+    field = None        # "msgid" or "msgstr" while reading continuation lines
+    parts = {}
+
+    def finish():
+        nonlocal cur, field, parts, header
+        if cur is None:
+            return
+        if "msgid" not in parts or "msgstr" not in parts:
+            raise PoError(f"{path}:{cur.line}: entry without msgid and msgstr")
+        cur.msgid = "".join(parts["msgid"])
+        cur.msgstr = "".join(parts["msgstr"])
+        if cur.msgid == "" and not cur.obsolete:
+            header = cur
+        else:
+            entries.append(cur)
+        cur, field, parts = None, None, {}
+
+    for n, raw in enumerate(lines, 1):
+        line = raw.strip()
+        obsolete = False
+        if line.startswith("#~"):
+            obsolete = True
+            line = line[2:].strip()
+            if not line:
+                continue
+        if not line:
+            finish()
+            continue
+        if line.startswith("#") and not obsolete:
+            if cur is not None and "msgid" in parts:
+                finish()
+            if cur is None:
+                cur = Entry(msgid="", line=n)
+            kind, text = line[:2], line[2:].strip()
+            if kind == "#.":
+                cur.extracted.append(text)
+            elif kind == "#:":
+                cur.references.extend(text.split())
+            elif kind == "#,":
+                cur.flags.extend(f.strip() for f in text.split(",") if f.strip())
+            elif kind == "#|":
+                pass  # previous msgid of a fuzzy entry: not kept
+            else:
+                cur.comments.append(line[1:].strip())
+            continue
+        m = re.match(r'^(msgctxt|msgid_plural|msgid|msgstr(?:\[\d+\])?)\s+"(.*)"$', line)
+        if m:
+            key, body = m.group(1), m.group(2)
+            if key in ("msgctxt", "msgid_plural") or key.startswith("msgstr["):
+                raise PoError(f"{path}:{n}: {key} is not supported (no contexts or plurals)")
+            if key == "msgid":
+                if cur is not None and "msgid" in parts:
+                    finish()
+                if cur is None:
+                    cur = Entry(msgid="", line=n)
+                cur.line = n
+                cur.obsolete = obsolete
+            elif cur is None or "msgid" not in parts:
+                raise PoError(f"{path}:{n}: msgstr without msgid")
+            field = key
+            parts[field] = [unescape(body, path, n)]
+            continue
+        m = re.match(r'^"(.*)"$', line)
+        if m and field is not None:
+            parts[field].append(unescape(m.group(1), path, n))
+            continue
+        raise PoError(f"{path}:{n}: cannot read this line: {raw!r}")
+    finish()
+    return header, entries
+
+
+def header_fields(header) -> dict:
+    fields = {}
+    if header is not None:
+        for line in header.msgstr.split("\n"):
+            if ":" in line:
+                k, v = line.split(":", 1)
+                fields[k.strip()] = v.strip()
+    return fields
+
+
+def make_header(fields: dict, comments=()) -> Entry:
+    return Entry(msgid="", msgstr="".join(f"{k}: {v}\n" for k, v in fields.items()), comments=list(comments))
+
+
+def _string_lines(key: str, text: str, prefix: str) -> list:
+    pieces = re.findall(r"[^\n]*\n|[^\n]+", text)
+    if len(pieces) <= 1:
+        return [f'{prefix}{key} "{escape(text)}"']
+    return [f'{prefix}{key} ""'] + [f'{prefix}"{escape(p)}"' for p in pieces]
+
+
+def format_entry(e: Entry) -> str:
+    out = []
+    for c in e.comments:
+        out.append(f"# {c}".rstrip())
+    for c in e.extracted:
+        out.append(f"#. {c}")
+    if e.references:
+        out.append("#: " + " ".join(e.references))
+    if e.flags:
+        out.append("#, " + ", ".join(e.flags))
+    prefix = "#~ " if e.obsolete else ""
+    out += _string_lines("msgid", e.msgid, prefix)
+    out += _string_lines("msgstr", e.msgstr, prefix)
+    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"
+
+
+def write(path: str, header, entries) -> None:
+    blocks = []
+    if header is not None:
+        blocks.append(format_entry(header))
+    blocks += [format_entry(e) for e in entries]
+    with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
+        f.write("\n".join(blocks))
+
+
+_SPEC = re.compile(r"%(?:%|[-+ #0]*(?:\*|\d+)?(?:\.(?:\*|\d*))?(?:hh|h|ll|l|L|z|j|t|I64|I32|I)?[diouxXeEfFgGaAcspn])")
+
+
+def format_specs(text: str) -> list:
+    """The printf conversions of text in order, without the %% escapes."""
+    return [m.group(0) for m in _SPEC.finditer(text) if m.group(0) != "%%"]
+
+
+def stray_percent(text: str) -> bool:
+    """True when text has a % that is neither %% nor a complete conversion."""
+    return "%" in _SPEC.sub("", text)
diff --git a/i18n/tools/subset_fonts.py b/i18n/tools/subset_fonts.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..efe23b6e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/i18n/tools/subset_fonts.py
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+"""Rebuilds the CJK fonts in i18n/fonts from the full Noto Sans fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
+
+The menus draw Latin and Cyrillic with NVIDIA Sans; Chinese, Japanese and Korean need these fonts.
+Each one keeps a common character set of its language (so most edits to a .po file need no new
+glyphs) plus every character the translations that use it contain. The build fails with
+"... have no glyph for ..." when a translation uses a character outside its font; run this then.
+
+Needs fontTools (python -m pip install fonttools) and the source fonts, Noto Sans SC, TC, JP and KR
+Regular (OTF), for example from https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk (Sans/SubsetOTF) or the copies
+SteamVR ships in tools/steamvr_environments/game/steamtours/panorama/fonts.
+
+Usage: python i18n/tools/subset_fonts.py [--source-dir <folder with the four fonts>]
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import os
+import sys
+
+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
+import po  # noqa: E402
+
+ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
+I18N = os.path.join(ROOT, "i18n")
+FONTS = os.path.join(I18N, "fonts")
+STEAMVR = r"C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\SteamVR\tools\steamvr_environments\game\steamtours\panorama\fonts"
+
+# Output font -> (source file names to look for, codec and lead/trail byte ranges of the common character set)
+SOURCES = {
+    "NotoSansSC": (["notosanssc-regular.otf", "NotoSansSC-Regular.otf", "NotoSansCJKsc-Regular.otf"],
+                   "gb2312", (0xA1, 0xF7), [(0xA1, 0xFE)]),                       # GB 2312: 6,763 hanzi
+    "NotoSansTC": (["notosanstc-regular.otf", "NotoSansTC-Regular.otf", "NotoSansCJKtc-Regular.otf"],
+                   "big5", (0xA1, 0xC6), [(0x40, 0x7E), (0xA1, 0xFE)]),            # Big5 symbols and the 5,401 frequent hanzi
+    "NotoSansJP": (["notosansjp-regular.otf", "NotoSansJP-Regular.otf", "NotoSansCJKjp-Regular.otf"],
+                   "euc_jp", (0xA1, 0xF4), [(0xA1, 0xFE)]),                       # JIS X 0208: kana and 6,355 kanji
+    "NotoSansKR": (["notosanskr-regular.otf", "NotoSansKR-Regular.otf", "NotoSansCJKkr-Regular.otf"],
+                   "euc_kr", (0xA1, 0xFE), [(0xA1, 0xFE)]),                       # KS X 1001 without hanja: 2,350 hangul syllables
+}
+
+
+def charset(codec, lead, trails):
+    chars = set(range(0x20, 0x7F))
+    for a in range(lead[0], lead[1] + 1):
+        for lo, hi in trails:
+            for b in range(lo, hi + 1):
+                try:
+                    text = bytes((a, b)).decode(codec)
+                except UnicodeDecodeError:
+                    continue
+                chars.update(ord(c) for c in text)
+    return chars
+
+
+def used_characters():
+    """Characters of each font's languages: their translations and their names."""
+    used = {}
+    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(I18N)):
+        if not fn.endswith(".po"):
+            continue
+        header, entries = po.parse(os.path.join(I18N, fn))
+        fields = po.header_fields(header)
+        font = fields.get("X-Remix-Font", "")
+        if not font:
+            continue
+        chars = used.setdefault(font, set())
+        chars.update(ord(c) for c in fields.get("X-Remix-Language-Name", ""))
+        for e in entries:
+            if not e.obsolete:
+                chars.update(ord(c) for c in e.msgstr if ord(c) >= 0x20)
+    return used
+
+
+def main():
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
+    ap.add_argument("--source-dir", default=STEAMVR if os.path.isdir(STEAMVR) else None,
+                    help="folder holding Noto Sans SC, TC, JP and KR Regular (.otf)")
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+    try:
+        from fontTools import subset
+        from fontTools.ttLib import TTFont
+    except ImportError:
+        print("fontTools is missing: python -m pip install fonttools", file=sys.stderr)
+        return 1
+    if not args.source_dir:
+        print("give --source-dir: the folder with the Noto Sans SC, TC, JP and KR fonts", file=sys.stderr)
+        return 1
+
+    used = used_characters()
+    os.makedirs(FONTS, exist_ok=True)
+    for name, (candidates, codec, lead, trails) in SOURCES.items():
+        source = next((os.path.join(args.source_dir, c) for c in candidates
+                       if os.path.exists(os.path.join(args.source_dir, c))), None)
+        if source is None:
+            print(f"{name}: none of {', '.join(candidates)} in {args.source_dir}", file=sys.stderr)
+            return 1
+        font = TTFont(source)
+        cmap = font.getBestCmap()
+        wanted = charset(codec, lead, trails) | {c for c in range(0x3000, 0x3040)} | {c for c in range(0xFF01, 0xFF5F)}
+        if name == "NotoSansKR":
+            wanted = {c for c in wanted if not (0x4E00 <= c <= 0x9FFF or 0xF900 <= c <= 0xFAFF)}
+        needed = used.get(name, set())
+        missing = sorted(c for c in needed if c not in cmap)
+        if missing:
+            print(f"warning: {os.path.basename(source)} has no glyph for "
+                  + " ".join(f"U+{c:04X}" for c in missing), file=sys.stderr)
+        unicodes = sorted(c for c in (wanted | needed) if c in cmap and c <= 0xFFFF)
+
+        options = subset.Options()
+        options.layout_features = []
+        options.hinting = False
+        options.name_IDs = ["*"]
+        options.name_languages = ["*"]
+        options.notdef_outline = True
+        options.drop_tables += ["GSUB", "GPOS", "GDEF", "BASE", "VORG", "vhea", "vmtx", "DSIG"]
+        subsetter = subset.Subsetter(options=options)
+        subsetter.populate(unicodes=unicodes)
+        subsetter.subset(font)
+        out = os.path.join(FONTS, name + ".otf")
+        font.save(out)
+        print(f"{name}: {len(unicodes)} characters, {os.path.getsize(out):,} bytes from {os.path.basename(source)}")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main())
diff --git a/i18n/tools/update_strings.py b/i18n/tools/update_strings.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b0564275
--- /dev/null
+++ b/i18n/tools/update_strings.py
@@ -0,0 +1,511 @@
+"""Extracts the English text of the Remix menus from the C++ sources into i18n/remix.pot and merges
+it into every i18n/<language>.po.
+
+What counts as menu text:
+- string literals passed to ImGui and RemixGui widgets in their label, text and tooltip positions;
+- combo box entries (RemixGui::ComboWithKey initializers, "a\\0b\\0" item lists, const char* arrays);
+- the descriptions of the rtx.* options that a menu binds to a widget (their xxxObject() accessor
+  appears in a file that draws ImGui), shown in the option's tooltip.
+
+Merging keeps every existing translation, adds new text with an empty msgstr (the menu shows the
+English text until it is translated) and keeps text that left the sources as obsolete "#~" entries,
+so nothing a translator wrote is lost.
+
+Usage: python i18n/tools/update_strings.py [--check]
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import bisect
+import os
+import re
+import sys
+
+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
+import po  # noqa: E402
+
+ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
+I18N = os.path.join(ROOT, "i18n")
+POT = os.path.join(I18N, "remix.pot")
+
+# Sources that are not menu text: vendored ImGui/ImPlot and their demos.
+SKIP_FILES = {"imgui.cpp", "imgui_widgets.cpp", "imgui_draw.cpp", "imgui_tables.cpp", "imgui_demo.cpp",
+              "implot.cpp", "implot_items.cpp", "implot_demo.cpp", "imgui_impl_win32.cpp", "imgui_remix_exports.cpp"}
+
+# Widgets whose first argument is a visible label.
+LABEL_FUNCS = {
+    "Button", "SmallButton", "Checkbox", "CheckboxFlags", "RadioButton", "Combo", "BeginCombo", "Selectable",
+    "MenuItem", "BeginMenu", "CollapsingHeader", "TreeNode", "TreeNodeEx", "BeginTabItem", "TabItemButton",
+    "InputText", "InputTextMultiline", "InputTextWithHint", "InputFloat", "InputFloat2", "InputFloat3",
+    "InputFloat4", "InputInt", "InputInt2", "InputInt3", "InputInt4", "InputDouble", "InputScalar",
+    "InputScalarN", "DragFloat", "DragFloat2", "DragFloat3", "DragFloat4", "DragFloatRange2", "DragInt",
+    "DragInt2", "DragInt3", "DragInt4", "DragIntRange2", "DragScalar", "DragScalarN", "SliderFloat",
+    "SliderFloat2", "SliderFloat3", "SliderFloat4", "SliderAngle", "SliderInt", "SliderInt2", "SliderInt3",
+    "SliderInt4", "SliderScalar", "SliderScalarN", "VSliderFloat", "VSliderInt", "VSliderScalar", "ColorEdit3",
+    "ColorEdit4", "ColorPicker3", "ColorPicker4", "ListBox", "BeginListBox", "PlotLines", "PlotHistogram",
+    "Begin", "BeginPopupModal", "TableSetupColumn", "TableHeader", "TextSeparator", "SeparatorText", "Value",
+    "ComboWithKey", "Separator", "TextLinkOpenURL", "Hyperlink",
+}
+# Widgets whose every string argument is shown (labels, previews, hints, overlay text, item lists).
+ALL_ARGS_FUNCS = {"BeginCombo", "InputTextWithHint", "MenuItem", "ProgressBar", "LabelText", "Combo", "ListBox",
+                  "TreeNode", "TreeNodeEx", "PlotLines", "PlotHistogram", "Selectable"}
+# printf-style text: the first string is a format, the others are %s arguments shown as they are.
+FORMAT_FUNCS = {"Text": 0, "TextDisabled": 0, "TextWrapped": 0, "BulletText": 0, "SetTooltip": 0, "TextColored": 1,
+                "LabelText": 1, "TextCentered": 0, "TextWrappedCentered": 0, "LogText": 0}
+TEXT_FUNCS = {"TextUnformatted": 0, "SetTooltipUnformatted": 0, "SetTooltipUnformattedUnwrapped": 0,
+              "SetTooltipToLastWidgetOnHover": 0, "IMGUI_ADD_TOOLTIP": 1, "addTooltipAndPassthroughValue": 1,
+              "AddText": None, "TextWithTooltip": None, "translateUiText": 0}
+# Text kept in a variable before it is drawn: `const char* tabDescriptionText = "..."`.
+TEXT_VARIABLE = re.compile(r"(?i)(text|desc|tooltip|label|title|message|hint)")
+# The menus' own helpers that draw a widget: dragFloatWithWeatherOverride("Label", ...), showLegacyGui(..., "Name", "Tooltip").
+HELPER_FUNC = re.compile(r"(?i)(slider|drag|checkbox|combo|color|edit|override|gui|row|label|tooltip|header|button|show|widget)")
+# Prose rather than an identifier: words with spaces, or one capitalised word.
+LOOKS_LIKE_TEXT = re.compile(r"\S\s+\S|^[A-Z][a-z]+[.:!?)]?$")
+# Calls whose strings are IDs or data, never shown.
+ID_FUNCS = {"PushID", "GetID", "BeginChild", "BeginTabBar", "OpenPopup", "BeginPopup", "BeginPopupContextItem",
+            "BeginPopupContextWindow", "IsPopupOpen", "BeginTable", "SetWindowFocus", "BeginDragDropSource",
+            "AcceptDragDropPayload", "SetDragDropPayload", "LoadIniSettingsFromDisk", "SaveIniSettingsToDisk",
+            "ScopedCpuProfileZone", "ScopedGpuProfileZone", "PushOverrideID", "FindWindowByName", "BeginTooltipEx"}
+LOG_FUNCS = {"info", "warn", "err", "debug", "trace", "Logger", "format", "throw", "DxvkError", "assert", "printf",
+             "sprintf", "snprintf", "OutputDebugStringA", "ONCE", "getenv", "Once", "logWarning", "logInfo",
+             "logError", "env", "Error", "fail", "strcmp", "strncmp", "find", "rfind", "compare", "starts_with",
+             "ends_with", "stoi", "stof", "fopen", "open", "ifstream", "ofstream", "path", "replace"}
+
+OPTION_MACROS = {"RTX_OPTION": 4, "RTX_OPTION_ARGS": 4, "RTX_OPTION_ENV": 5, "RTX_OPTION_FLAG": 5,
+                 "RTX_OPTION_FLAG_ENV": 6, "RTX_OPTION_FULL": 6}
+
+# Text a function returns that the menus pass through translateUiText; the extractor cannot see it.
+EXTRA_MESSAGES = {
+    "src/dxvk/rtx_render/rtx_dlss.cpp:41": [  # dlssProfileToString
+        "Ultra Performance", "Max Performance", "Balanced", "Max Quality", "Auto", "Full Resolution"],
+}
+
+TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r'''
+  (?P<ws>\s+)
+| (?P<comment>//[^\n]*|/\*.*?\*/)
+| (?P<raw>(?:u8|u|U|L)?R"(?P<delim>[^()\\\s]{0,16})\((?P<rawbody>.*?)\)(?P=delim)")
+| (?P<str>(?:u8|u|U|L)?"(?:[^"\\\n]|\\.)*")
+| (?P<chr>(?:u8|u|U|L)?'(?:[^'\\\n]|\\.)*')
+| (?P<ident>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)
+| (?P<num>\.?[0-9](?:[0-9a-zA-Z_.]|'[0-9a-zA-Z]|[eEpP][+-])*)
+| (?P<op>::|->|<<=|>>=|<<|>>|&&|\|\||[-+*/%&|^!=<>]=?|[{}()\[\];,.?:~\#@$\\])
+''', re.S | re.X)
+
+_C_ESC = {"n": "\n", "t": "\t", "r": "\r", "a": "\a", "b": "\b", "f": "\f", "v": "\v", "\\": "\\", '"': '"',
+          "'": "'", "?": "?"}
+
+KEYWORDS = {"if", "while", "for", "switch", "return", "sizeof", "case", "catch", "decltype", "alignof", "co_return",
+            "static_assert", "defined", "else", "do"}
+
+
+def decode_literal(tok: str) -> str:
+    body = tok[tok.index('"') + 1:-1]
+    out = []
+    i = 0
+    while i < len(body):
+        c = body[i]
+        if c != "\\":
+            out.append(c)
+            i += 1
+            continue
+        c = body[i + 1]
+        if c in _C_ESC:
+            out.append(_C_ESC[c])
+            i += 2
+        elif c == "x":
+            m = re.match(r"[0-9a-fA-F]+", body[i + 2:])
+            out.append(chr(int(m.group(0), 16)))
+            i += 2 + len(m.group(0))
+        elif c in "01234567":
+            m = re.match(r"[0-7]{1,3}", body[i + 1:])
+            out.append(chr(int(m.group(0), 8)))
+            i += 1 + len(m.group(0))
+        elif c in "uU":
+            n = 4 if c == "u" else 8
+            out.append(chr(int(body[i + 2:i + 2 + n], 16)))
+            i += 2 + n
+        else:
+            out.append(c)
+            i += 2
+    return "".join(out)
+
+
+def blank_preprocessor(text: str) -> str:
+    out = []
+    cont = False
+    for line in text.split("\n"):
+        if cont or line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
+            cont = line.rstrip().endswith("\\")
+            out.append("")
+        else:
+            out.append(line)
+    return "\n".join(out)
+
+
+class Tok:
+    __slots__ = ("kind", "value", "line")
+
+    def __init__(self, kind, value, line):
+        self.kind, self.value, self.line = kind, value, line
+
+
+def tokenize(path: str):
+    with open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
+        text = blank_preprocessor(f.read())
+    newlines = [m.start() for m in re.finditer("\n", text)]
+    toks = []
+    pos = 0
+    while pos < len(text):
+        m = TOKEN_RE.match(text, pos)
+        if not m:
+            pos += 1
+            continue
+        kind = m.lastgroup
+        if kind == "delim" or kind == "rawbody":
+            kind = "raw"
+        if kind not in ("ws", "comment"):
+            line = bisect.bisect_right(newlines, m.start()) + 1
+            if m.group("raw"):
+                toks.append(Tok("str", m.group("rawbody"), line))
+            elif kind == "str":
+                toks.append(Tok("str", decode_literal(m.group(0)), line))
+            else:
+                toks.append(Tok(kind, m.group(0), line))
+        pos = m.end()
+    # Join adjacent literals, as the compiler does.
+    joined = []
+    for t in toks:
+        if t.kind == "str" and joined and joined[-1].kind == "str":
+            joined[-1] = Tok("str", joined[-1].value + t.value, joined[-1].line)
+        else:
+            joined.append(t)
+    return joined
+
+
+class Frame:
+    __slots__ = ("kind", "callee", "qual", "arg", "context")
+
+    def __init__(self, kind, callee, qual, context):
+        self.kind, self.callee, self.qual, self.arg, self.context = kind, callee, qual, 0, context
+
+
+def callee_before(toks, i):
+    """Name and qualified name of the function or type right before toks[i] (an opening bracket)."""
+    j = i - 1
+    if j >= 0 and toks[j].value == ">":
+        depth = 0
+        while j >= 0:
+            if toks[j].value == ">":
+                depth += 1
+            elif toks[j].value == ">>":
+                depth += 2
+            elif toks[j].value == "<":
+                depth -= 1
+                if depth == 0:
+                    break
+            elif toks[j].value in (";", "{", "}"):
+                return None, None
+            j -= 1
+        j -= 1
+    if j < 0 or toks[j].kind != "ident" or toks[j].value in KEYWORDS:
+        return None, None
+    name = toks[j].value
+    qual = [name]
+    while j >= 2 and toks[j - 1].value == "::" and toks[j - 2].kind == "ident":
+        qual.insert(0, toks[j - 2].value)
+        j -= 2
+    return name, "::".join(qual)
+
+
+def context_before(toks, i, n=14):
+    words = []
+    for t in toks[max(0, i - n):i]:
+        if t.value in (";", "}"):
+            words = []
+        else:
+            words.append(t.value)
+    return words
+
+
+class Extractor:
+    def __init__(self):
+        self.messages = {}      # msgid -> {"refs": [], "flags": set(), "notes": []}
+        self.accessors = set()  # names X of every XObject() used where menus are drawn
+        self.options = []       # (fullname, accessor name, description, ref)
+
+    def add(self, text, ref, fmt=False, note=None):
+        text = text.split("##", 1)[0] if "##" in text else text
+        if not re.search(r"[A-Za-z]", text) or re.search(r"[\x00-\x08\x0b-\x1f\x7f]", text):
+            return
+        stripped = po._SPEC.sub("", text)
+        if not re.search(r"[A-Za-z]{2}", stripped):
+            return
+        if text.startswith("__") or re.fullmatch(r"[_a-z][\w]*(\.[\w\[\]*]+)+", text):
+            return  # an option or API key, not prose
+        if text.startswith("%") and len(re.findall(r"[A-Za-z]", stripped)) <= 3:
+            return  # a value format such as "%.2f km": the drawn value never matches a message
+        msg = self.messages.setdefault(text, {"refs": [], "flags": set(), "notes": []})
+        if ref not in msg["refs"]:
+            msg["refs"].append(ref)
+        if fmt:
+            msg["flags"].add("c-format")
+        if note and note not in msg["notes"]:
+            msg["notes"].append(note)
+
+    def scan_file(self, path, rel):
+        toks = tokenize(path)
+        is_ui = any(t.kind == "ident" and (t.value.startswith(("ImGui", "ImPlot", "RemixGui")) or t.value == "ImGUI")
+                    for t in toks)
+        if is_ui:
+            for i, t in enumerate(toks):
+                if t.kind == "ident" and t.value.endswith("Object") and len(t.value) > 6 \
+                        and i + 2 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1].value == "(" and toks[i + 2].value == ")":
+                    self.accessors.add(t.value[:-6])
+        self.scan_options(toks, rel)
+        if is_ui:
+            self.scan_ui(toks, rel)
+
+    def scan_options(self, toks, rel):
+        i = 0
+        while i < len(toks):
+            t = toks[i]
+            if t.kind == "ident" and t.value in OPTION_MACROS and i + 1 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1].value == "(":
+                args, j = self.split_args(toks, i + 1)
+                index = OPTION_MACROS[t.value]
+                if len(args) > index and args[0] and args[0][0].kind == "str" and len(args[2]) == 1:
+                    desc = [a for a in args[index] if a.kind == "str"]
+                    if len(desc) == 1 and len(args[index]) == 1:
+                        full = f"{args[0][0].value}.{args[2][0].value}"
+                        self.options.append((full, args[2][0].value, desc[0].value, f"{rel}:{t.line}"))
+                i = j
+            i += 1
+
+    @staticmethod
+    def split_args(toks, open_index):
+        args, cur, depth = [], [], 0
+        j = open_index
+        while j < len(toks):
+            v = toks[j].value
+            if v in ("(", "{", "["):
+                depth += 1
+                if depth > 1:
+                    cur.append(toks[j])
+            elif v in (")", "}", "]"):
+                depth -= 1
+                if depth == 0:
+                    args.append(cur)
+                    return args, j
+                cur.append(toks[j])
+            elif v == "," and depth == 1:
+                args.append(cur)
+                cur = []
+            else:
+                cur.append(toks[j])
+            j += 1
+        return args, j
+
+    def scan_ui(self, toks, rel):
+        stack = []
+        for i, t in enumerate(toks):
+            v = t.value
+            if t.kind == "op" and v in ("(", "{", "["):
+                name, qual = callee_before(toks, i) if v != "[" else (None, None)
+                stack.append(Frame(v, name, qual, context_before(toks, i) if v == "{" else None))
+            elif t.kind == "op" and v in (")", "}", "]"):
+                if stack:
+                    stack.pop()
+            elif t.kind == "op" and v == "," and stack:
+                stack[-1].arg += 1
+            elif t.kind == "str":
+                self.classify(stack, t, toks, i, rel)
+
+    def classify(self, stack, t, toks, i, rel):
+        ref = f"{rel}:{t.line}"
+        text = t.value
+        # "0x%" PRIx64: the text the code draws is completed by a macro, so this literal never matches it.
+        if (i + 1 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1].kind == "ident" and toks[i + 1].value.startswith("PRI")) or \
+                (i >= 1 and toks[i - 1].kind == "ident" and toks[i - 1].value.startswith("PRI")):
+            return
+        # std::string("Save##") + id: a widget label, whatever builds it.
+        if "##" in text and not text.startswith("##"):
+            self.add(text, ref)
+            return
+        if i >= 2 and toks[i - 1].value == "=" and toks[i - 2].kind == "ident" and TEXT_VARIABLE.search(toks[i - 2].value):
+            self.add(text, ref)
+            return
+        if not stack:
+            return
+        top = stack[-1]
+        # Combo item lists given as "a\0b\0c\0".
+        if "\0" in text:
+            if top.kind == "(" and top.callee in ("Combo", "ListBox"):
+                for item in text.split("\0"):
+                    self.add(item, ref)
+            return
+        if top.kind == "(":
+            name = top.callee
+            if name is None:
+                # A parenthesised expression: look through it to the call around it.
+                for f in reversed(stack[:-1]):
+                    if f.kind == "(" and f.callee is not None:
+                        top = f
+                        name = f.callee
+                        break
+                    if f.kind != "(":
+                        break
+                if name is None:
+                    return
+            if name in ID_FUNCS or name in LOG_FUNCS:
+                return
+            if name in FORMAT_FUNCS:
+                self.add(text, ref, fmt=(top.arg == FORMAT_FUNCS[name]))
+            elif name in TEXT_FUNCS:
+                want = TEXT_FUNCS[name]
+                if want is None or top.arg == want:
+                    self.add(text, ref)
+            elif name in ALL_ARGS_FUNCS:
+                self.add(text, ref)
+            elif name in LABEL_FUNCS:
+                if top.arg == 0:
+                    self.add(text, ref)
+            elif top.qual and top.qual.startswith("RemixGui::"):
+                self.add(text, ref)
+            elif HELPER_FUNC.search(name) and LOOKS_LIKE_TEXT.search(text):
+                self.add(text, ref)
+            return
+        if top.kind == "{":
+            for f in reversed(stack):
+                words = (f.context or []) + ([f.callee] if f.callee else [])
+                if any(w in ("ComboWithKey", "ComboEntries") for w in words):
+                    self.add(text, ref)
+                    return
+                if "char" in words and "[" in words and "=" in words:
+                    self.add(text, ref)
+                    return
+                # A table of entries, such as the texture categories: {"uitextures", "UI Texture", &...}.
+                if "=" in words and LOOKS_LIKE_TEXT.search(text):
+                    self.add(text, ref)
+                    return
+                if f.kind == "(" and f.callee:
+                    break
+
+    def option_messages(self):
+        for full, accessor, desc, ref in self.options:
+            if accessor in self.accessors and desc.strip():
+                self.add(desc, ref, note=full)
+        for ref, texts in EXTRA_MESSAGES.items():
+            for text in texts:
+                self.add(text, ref)
+
+
+def scan_sources():
+    ex = Extractor()
+    for base in ("src",):
+        for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(os.path.join(ROOT, base)):
+            dirnames.sort()
+            if "usd-plugins" in dirpath or os.sep + "_external" in dirpath:
+                continue
+            for fn in sorted(filenames):
+                if not fn.endswith((".cpp", ".h", ".hpp", ".inl")) or fn in SKIP_FILES or fn.startswith("imstb"):
+                    continue
+                path = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)
+                rel = os.path.relpath(path, ROOT).replace(os.sep, "/")
+                ex.scan_file(path, rel)
+    ex.option_messages()
+    return ex
+
+
+def build_pot(ex):
+    entries = []
+    for text, info in ex.messages.items():
+        flags = sorted(info["flags"])
+        entries.append(po.Entry(msgid=text, extracted=[f"option {n}" for n in info["notes"]],
+                                references=info["refs"], flags=flags))
+
+    def key(e):
+        f, _, line = e.references[0].rpartition(":")
+        return (f, int(line), e.msgid)
+    entries.sort(key=key)
+    header = po.make_header({
+        "Project-Id-Version": "dxvk-remix-gmod",
+        "MIME-Version": "1.0",
+        "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=UTF-8",
+        "Content-Transfer-Encoding": "8bit",
+    }, comments=["English text of the RTX Remix menus. Generated by i18n/tools/update_strings.py; do not edit.",
+                 "Translate in i18n/<language>.po; see i18n/README.md."])
+    return header, entries
+
+
+def merge(po_path, pot_entries):
+    header, old = po.parse(po_path)
+    old_by_id = {e.msgid: e for e in old}
+    merged = []
+    for t in pot_entries:
+        o = old_by_id.pop(t.msgid, None)
+        e = po.Entry(msgid=t.msgid, extracted=list(t.extracted), references=list(t.references), flags=list(t.flags))
+        if o is not None:
+            e.msgstr = o.msgstr
+            e.comments = list(o.comments)
+            if "fuzzy" in o.flags:
+                e.flags.append("fuzzy")
+        merged.append(e)
+    obsolete = []
+    for o in old_by_id.values():
+        if o.msgstr:
+            obsolete.append(po.Entry(msgid=o.msgid, msgstr=o.msgstr, comments=list(o.comments), obsolete=True))
+    return header, merged + obsolete
+
+
+def main():
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
+    ap.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="only report whether remix.pot is current (exit 1 if not)")
+    ap.add_argument("--stats", action="store_true", help="print counts of extracted text")
+    ap.add_argument("--new-language", metavar="CODE", help="also start i18n/CODE.po (GMod's language code, e.g. de)")
+    ap.add_argument("--name", help="with --new-language: the language's name in itself, e.g. Deutsch")
+    ap.add_argument("--font", default="", help="with --new-language: font in i18n/fonts for characters NVIDIA Sans lacks")
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+
+    if args.new_language:
+        path = os.path.join(I18N, args.new_language + ".po")
+        if os.path.exists(path) or not args.name:
+            print(f"{path} exists, or --name is missing")
+            return 1
+        fields = {"Project-Id-Version": "dxvk-remix-gmod", "Language": args.new_language, "MIME-Version": "1.0",
+                  "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=UTF-8", "Content-Transfer-Encoding": "8bit",
+                  "X-Remix-Language-Name": args.name, "X-Remix-Font": args.font}
+        po.write(path, po.make_header(fields, comments=[f"{args.name} translation of the RTX Remix menus. See i18n/README.md."]), [])
+
+    ex = scan_sources()
+    header, entries = build_pot(ex)
+    if args.stats:
+        opts = sum(1 for e in entries if e.extracted)
+        words = sum(len(e.msgid.split()) for e in entries)
+        print(f"{len(entries)} messages ({opts} option descriptions), {words} words; "
+              f"{len(ex.options)} options declared, {len(ex.accessors)} accessors used by menus")
+    if args.check:
+        tmp = POT + ".check"
+        po.write(tmp, header, entries)
+        with open(tmp, "rb") as a:
+            new = a.read()
+        os.remove(tmp)
+        old = open(POT, "rb").read() if os.path.exists(POT) else b""
+        if new != old:
+            print("i18n/remix.pot is out of date: run python i18n/tools/update_strings.py")
+            return 1
+        return 0
+
+    po.write(POT, header, entries)
+    print(f"wrote {os.path.relpath(POT, ROOT)}: {len(entries)} messages")
+    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(I18N)):
+        if fn.endswith(".po"):
+            path = os.path.join(I18N, fn)
+            h, merged = merge(path, entries)
+            po.write(path, h, merged)
+            todo = sum(1 for e in merged if not e.obsolete and not e.msgstr)
+            print(f"merged {fn}: {todo} untranslated, {sum(1 for e in merged if e.obsolete)} obsolete")
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    sys.exit(main())
diff --git a/i18n/zh-CN.po b/i18n/zh-CN.po
